  chapterSnapshot: 'NCERT Class 6 Science (Curiosity) Chapter 10: Living Creatures: Exploring their Characteristics (QR: 0677CH10, pp. 183-206). Explores the universal hallmarks of living organisms versus non-living things through experiential inquiry. Opens with Avadhi and Aayush discovering a living snail within an apparently lifeless shell. Systematically details core life processes: nutrition, respiration (distinguishing physical breathing from cellular respiration and leaf stomata gas exchange), irreversible growth, metabolic excretion (sweat, urine, plant guttation droplets), response to stimuli (Mimosa pudica/chhui-mui thigmonasty, amla nyctinasty, phototropism, geotropism), reproduction for continuity of life, and biological death. Investigates seed biology, establishing seed dormancy and the universal requirements for germination (water and air/oxygen in soil spaces), noting species-specific photoperiod requirements (Coleus/Petunia require light; Calendula/Zinnia require darkness). Details Sir J. C. Bose\'s invention of the Crescograph proving plant sensitivity. Traces plant development across 5 stages in bean plants and animal metamorphosis across mosquitoes (Egg -> Larva -> Pupa -> Adult; kerosene barrier mechanism), frogs (Spawn -> Gilled Aquatic Tadpole -> Froglet -> Amphibious Lungs/Skin Adult), and silk moths (Egg -> Silkworm -> Cocoon/Pupa -> Adult Moth; KVIC sericulture).',
